"# Builder 2g report: the review panel and the session bar\n\nI implemented 2g as described in §1.1, §5.1–5.9 and §5.13 of the plan, plus the three carry-overs. Only webview files changed: no core, runner or extension file, so §0's rule holds. The old stepper still works while `session` is null. Everything compiles, and every unit suite passes. The drafted Playwright spec passes too: I ran it against a build in my scratch dir, along with 6 existing related specs.\n\n## Carry-overs (2f's review)\n- **F-F3: not fixed, kept as recorded by fixer 2f r1 (\"the Apply write is treated as atomic\").** I re-checked this in code:\n  - `sessionEnd.ts` sends one change set (`[...plan.changes, ...sidecars]`) to `proposals.apply`.\n  - The extension's `CheckedEditApplier` applies it as one WorkspaceEdit, then saves file by file. So the gap only opens if the window closes between two saves.\n  - The finding's first option is worse than the gap. Treating this case as \"neither F nor B\" records drift on the files Apply wrote, and Apply stays disabled until the user reverts them by hand or exits. The gap itself only costs a cautious \"needs your endorsement\" flag.\n  - Writing the missing sidecars during recovery would put them outside Apply's history entry, so Undo would leave them behind (against D2-18).\n  - No behaviour changed, so there is no test. Recorded in §8.\n- **A-F4: not fixed.** Same defect and same decision as F-F3.\n- **F-F4: not fixed.** The `submitReview` toast is builder 2e's recorded decision and has its own test. Recorded in §8.\n\n## Files changed\n**New**\n- `packages/webview/src/state/session.ts` — the session slice (state, actions, its `receive` and `result` hooks), `sessionOverlay`, and the reader for the persisted review state.\n- `packages/webview/src/model/review.ts` — list rows, labels with provenance, statuses and badges, group previews (calling core's `planGroupAccept`/`planGroupDecline`), decline-menu entries, inference lines, the report model, control models, `reviewKey`, `paneModeFor`, and `agentPhrases`/`markAgent`.\n- `packages/webview/src/model/sessionBar.ts` — `sessionBarState`, the heading line, the badge text, the Exit counts, `confirmationModel`.\n- `packages/webview/src/run/SessionBar.tsx` — the session bar.\n- `packages/webview/src/run/review/parts.tsx` — Label, ItemLink, Marked, CardWords, StatusMark, Badges, Spinner.\n- `packages/webview/src/run/review/DeclineMenu.tsx`\n- `packages/webview/src/run/review/ItemDetail.tsx`\n- `packages/webview/src/run/review/ReviewList.tsx` — the list header, the listbox and the list/detail layout.\n- `packages/webview/src/run/review/StageReport.tsx` — Inferences, StageReport, EventsBox, RejectedList.\n- `packages/webview/src/run/review/EndConfirmation.tsx`\n- `packages/webview/test/shared/sessions.ts` — SessionView fixtures and `hiddenPair`.\n- `packages/webview/test/unit/review.test.ts`\n- `packages/webview/test/unit/sessionBar.test.ts`\n- `packages/webview/test/unit/store-session.test.ts`\n- `packages/webview/test/e2e/s2-review.spec.ts` (drafted; I also ran it)\n\n**Changed**\n- `packages/webview/src/state/store.ts` — wiring: `actionResult` goes to the session slice first; a `session` message case; the session overlay is kept through `proposal: null` and new graphs; session dialogs added to `DialogState`; `BoardActions` extends `SessionActions`; `PersistedState.sessionReview`.\n- `packages/webview/src/run/RunPanel.tsx` — session mode (\"Edit session\"); the \"Applied: …\" text after a session's Apply.\n- `packages/webview/src/run/RunBadge.tsx` — session badge texts; RunElsewhere for a session on another subject.\n- `packages/webview/src/dialogs/Dialogs.tsx` — the cascade, reveal, hold-as and exit-session dialogs.\n- `packages/webview/src/App.tsx` — adds `<SessionBar />`.\n- `packages/webview/src/main.tsx` — reads the persisted `sessionReview`.\n- `packages/webview/src/styles/board.css` — session bar and review panel styles (no style attributes).\n- `packages/webview/test/harness/harness.js` — auto-answers the session messages 2g posts.\n- `docs/slice2-plan.md` — §8 entry \"builder 2g\".\n\n## Tests\n- **Added (unit):**\n  - `review.test.ts`: 29 tests.\n  - `sessionBar.test.ts`: 12 tests.\n  - `store-session.test.ts`: 31 tests.\n  - They cover every §6.1 point for 2g, including the twin pair: two stores fed the proved and not-proved outcomes read equal rows, counts, report, controls and bar text.\n- **Added (Playwright):** `s2-review.spec.ts`, 10 tests: hidden stage, reveal and raw diff, Accept, the shown report and detail with Ask me instead, hold-as, read-only during a step, the end confirmation and Exit, narrow panel, a provenance check in the style of AT6.10, and the twin pair.\n- **Updated, skipped for later, moved, deleted:** none.\n\n## Verification\nAll runs used `S=/tmp/claude-1002/-home-zhengyew-telelean/c398a83b-d60f-46a4-ad9a-8d926e6fdd1b/scratchpad`, `B=$S/b2g`, and binaries from `/home/zhengyew/telelean/node_modules/.bin`, one heavy job at a time. MemAvailable stayed around 38 GB.\n\n- **Typecheck**, from the repo root: `$S/capped.sh 1800 …/tsc --noEmit -p <config>` for:\n  - `packages/core/tsconfig.test.json`\n  - `packages/runner/tsconfig.test.json`\n  - `packages/webview/tsconfig.json`\n  - `packages/webview/tsconfig.node.json`\n  - `packages/extension/tsconfig.json`\n\n  Each exited 0 with no output, both before and after the last change.\n- **Unit tests**, from `packages/<pkg>`: `TMPDIR=$B/tmp $S/capped.sh 1800 …/vitest run --maxWorkers=1 --no-cache --fsModuleCachePath=$B/fsmc`\n\n  | Package | Files | Summary line |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | core | 76 | `Tests  1134 passed (1134)` |\n  | webview | 22 | `Tests  387 passed (387)` (was 315) |\n  | extension | 22 | `Tests  219 passed (219)` |\n- **Runner smoke run** (no runner file changed; this covers the F-F3 area): `TELELEAN_TEST_TMP=$B/testtmp TMPDIR=$B/tmp $S/capped.sh 1800 timeout 900 …/vitest run --maxWorkers=1 --no-cache --fsModuleCachePath=$B/fsmc test/run/session.end.test.ts` → `Tests  35 passed (35)`.\n- **Build**, from `packages/webview`: `TMPDIR=$B/tmp TELELEAN_WEBVIEW_OUT=$B/webview-out $S/capped.sh 3000 …/vite build` → `✓ built in 450ms` (final sources). Output went only to the scratch dir; `git status` for `packages/extension/dist` and `out` is empty.\n- **Playwright**, from `packages/webview`: `TMPDIR=$B/tmp TELELEAN_TEST_RESULTS=$B/test-results TELELEAN_WEBVIEW_OUT=$B/webview-out $S/capped.sh 3000 sh -c 'ulimit -c 0; …/playwright test test/e2e/<spec>.spec.ts'`\n\n  | Spec | Result |\n  |---|---|\n  | s2-review | 10 passed |\n  | m2-review | 4 passed |\n  | m2-run | 5 passed |\n  | m2-provenance | 3 passed |\n  | s1-session | 2 passed |\n  | m2-overlay | 4 passed |\n  | m2-questions | 2 passed |\n\n  The home guard reported the real home unchanged every time. `packages/webview/test-results` was moved to `$B/test-results-playwright-dir2`.\n\n## Mutation checks\nEach mutant was applied in the source, the test files were run, and the file was restored and checked with `cmp`.\n\n**Result: 79 mutants, all caught.**\n- 71 on the slice, the store wiring and the two model files: 61 failed a test on the first run. The 10 survivors (S14, S23, S27, S28, S32, S33, R9, R17, B4, B11) got new tests or assertions, and all 10 then failed one.\n- 5 on the phrase marking (P1–P5): P5 survived, got a test, and now fails one.\n- 3 through the Playwright provenance check (E1–E3): all caught.\n\n| Mutant | File:line | What was broken | Test that failed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| S1 | state/session.ts:352 | `own: true` for a group | \"Select all in review\" then Accept, with one item, sends own: false |\n| S2 | :292 | read-only guard (D2-62) removed | no action that decides sends anything, in phases step and interrupted |\n| S3 | :292 | busy guard removed | busy blocks a second request |\n| S4 | :492 | arrow item declined with the option asked, not plain | arrow items decline plain (DO-0) |\n| S5 | :477 | written premise accepted as pending (AF12) | an Add premise already written … only as an axiom |\n| S6 | :812 | a confirmed request opens the cascade again | needs-confirmation opens the cascade dialog |\n| S7 | :822 | Accept & next does not move back on a refusal | Accept & next moves on at once, and back on a refusal |\n| S8 | :760 | `current` not kept across stages | a later stage keeps `current` |\n| S9 | :753 | persisted UI used for another run | the persisted UI is used only for the same run id |\n| S10 | :758 | a hidden Result stays selected | a later stage keeps `current` … selections dropped |\n| S11 | :780 | no switch to Proposed at the first stage | the first stage switches the board to Proposed |\n| S12 | :602 | raw diff sent without `confirmed` | Raw Lean diff…: the dialog first, then `confirmed` |\n| S13 | :662 | raw diff while hidden skips the dialog | Raw Lean diff…: the dialog first, then `confirmed` |\n| S14 | :637 | Apply before the check passed | Apply waits for a passed check with no drift |\n| S15 | :637 | Apply with drift | Apply waits for a passed check with no drift |\n| S16 | :639 | Apply without the check id | Submit, Apply, Back, Retry and Exit carry the right fields |\n| S17 | :627 | a second Exit while one is on its way | busy blocks a second request … Exit still goes, once |\n| S18 | :627 | Exit blocked by a decision on its way | busy blocks a second request … Exit still goes, once |\n| S19 | :677 | Undo sends the wrong step | session Undo and Redo send the step the user saw |\n| S20 | :372 | group Decline without `planGroupDecline` | a group sends one message … shows what was left |\n| S21 | :251 | Shaky's cascade worded as Reject's | needs-confirmation opens the cascade dialog |\n| S22 | :257 | Shaky note not trimmed | arrow items decline plain … Shaky with its note |\n| S23 | :507 | un-reject sends the item's rev | Un-reject sends the rejected version's rev |\n| S24 | :575 | \"Select these arrows\" keeps arrows that are not drawn | Select these arrows: drawn ones only |\n| S25 | :744 | `session: null` leaves the overlay | the session's board stays on screen … `session: null` clears it all |\n| S26 | :806 | no \"Left N\" note after a group | a group sends one message … shows what was left |\n| S27 | :514 | a hidden Result in a group Accept | nothing is sent for … a hidden Result in a group |\n| S28 | :459 | Accept on a closed gate | nothing is sent for an Accept its gate closes |\n| S29 | :460 | Add premise accepted without hold-as | an Add premise asks how it is held |\n| S30 | :704 | D on an arrow opens the menu | in a stage the same keys decide |\n| S31 | :776 | Exit dialog counts not refreshed | Submit, Apply, Back, Retry and Exit carry the right fields |\n| S32 | :771 | hold-as dialog stays after its item left review | the hold-as dialog closes when its item leaves review |\n| S33 | :364 | Shaky note sent with Reject | nothing is sent for … a note with Reject |\n| W1 | state/store.ts:1449 | session answers not routed to the slice | Accept & next moves on at once, and back on a refusal (10 tests failed) |\n| W2 | :1602 | `proposal: null` drops the session board | the session's board stays on screen |\n| W3 | :1773 | a new graph drops the session overlay | the session's board stays on screen |\n| W4 | :1697 | `session` message ignored | a new session starts its review UI … (25 tests failed) |\n| R1 | model/review.ts:162 | decline option missing from the status word | status as glyph and word … a decline names its option |\n| R2 | :255 | \"Only in review\" filter keeps everything | \"Only in review\" keeps the items in review |\n| R3 | :254 | rows reordered | keeps the host's order |\n| R4 | :325 | own-Accept class ignored | \"Accept N\", or \"Accept k of N\" |\n| R5 | :327 | a dependency refusal counted as blocked | \"Accept N\", or \"Accept k of N\" |\n| R6 | :336 | preview label always \"Accept N\" | \"Accept N\", or \"Accept k of N\" |\n| R7 | :356 | belief and changes-proved swapped in the note | the note lists what was left |\n| R8 | :412 | Shaky without its note field | the decline menu (§5.7) |\n| R9 | :627 | item controls open during a step | while a step runs they are closed even where a gate the host sent is open |\n| R10 | :654 | list controls open during a step | item, list, Un-reject and Ask me instead controls in phases step and interrupted |\n| R11 | :659 | group Accept enabled when it takes nothing | in a stage they follow the host's gates |\n| R12 | :668 | Un-reject offered on a superseded version | in a stage they follow the host's gates |\n| R13 | :590 | Ask me instead offers declined items | Ask me instead declines the items the choice names |\n| R14 | :746 | D on an arrow opens the menu | maps every review key |\n| R15 | :747 | R works outside the menu | maps every review key |\n| R16 | :753 | split from 600 px | paneModeFor |\n| R17 | :543 | verdict shown on a target marked unrevealed | the report: while hidden each target reads no verdict |\n| R18 | :466 | chip from the first step, not the latest | Inferences: … with the latest step's chip |\n| R19 | :234 | hidden Result selectable | a hidden Result is a neutral row |\n| R20 | :549 | a hint repeats a card the judgement names | a target not proved: the gap … with the board's hints |\n| R21 | :745 | Shift+A is a plain Accept | maps every review key |\n| R22 | :171 | \"depends on N\" badge missing | badges: belief, changes what is proved, depends on N |\n| B1 | model/sessionBar.ts:106 | Cancel step tooltip without the steps left | step: \"Claude's step for “T” (1 of 2)…\" |\n| B2 | :60 | \"did not pass\" text doubled | the ES-4 headings with Retry step |\n| B3 | :182 | Apply enabled with drift | Apply: enabled only on a passed check with no drift |\n| B4 | :182 | Apply enabled before the check passed | Apply: enabled only on a passed check with no drift |\n| B5 | :145 | badge says \"working\" in a stage | the badge never says proved or not proved |\n| B6 | :151 | Exit counts a hidden Result | the Exit dialog counts listed items only |\n| B7 | :110 | Submit tooltips swapped | the Submit texts |\n| B8 | :132 | Raw diff never asks first | stage: Raw Lean diff… asks first |\n| B9 | :127 | Resume enabled when the run cannot resume | interrupted: … Resume (enabled only when the run can resume) |\n| B10 | :130 | Retry enabled whatever its gate | the ES-4 headings with Retry step |\n| B11 | :135 | Submit enabled during a step | step: \"Claude's step for “T”…\" |\n| B12 | :96 | phase text lacks \"results after the review\" | the left side: the session, the stage, the phase text |\n| P1 | model/review.ts:73 | cut sentence forms not matched | Claude's phrases in the host's texts are marked as Claude's |\n| P2 | :96 | `markAgent` marks nothing | Claude's phrases in the host's texts are marked as Claude's |\n| P3 | :77 | Add premise sentence not one of Claude's phrases | Claude's phrases in the host's texts are marked as Claude's |\n| P4 | :508 | card provenance ignored | a card the board names carries who worded it |\n| P5 | :94 | a later phrase marked before an earlier one | Claude's phrases in the host's texts are marked as Claude's |\n| E1 | run/review/ItemDetail.tsx:391 | gate reason rendered as plain text | provenance (D-15) e2e test |\n| E2 | run/review/StageReport.tsx:271 | event item link rendered as plain text | provenance (D-15) e2e test |\n| E3 | run/SessionBar.tsx:145 | problem line rendered as plain text | provenance (D-15) e2e test |\n\nLines without a file name are in the file named on the row above.\n\n## Decisions for the orchestrator to log\nAll of these are also in the plan's §8 entry \"builder 2g\".\n\n1. **F-F3 and A-F4:** keep \"the Apply write is treated as atomic\". Alternative: treat \"model files equal F, a sidecar differs\" as the neither-case, as the finding offers.\n2. **F-F4:** keep the Submit review toast (2e's decision). Alternative: drop `submitReview` from `RUN_SUCCESS_NOTICES`.\n3. **Where the state lives:** a slice in `state/session.ts` spread into the store, with its own pending requests. The review UI is named `sessionReview`, because the legacy stepper's `review` stays until 2h. It is persisted as `{ runId, current, filter }` and reused only for the same run. Alternative: rename the legacy `review` now.\n4. **List order:** `reviewRows` keeps the host's order (2c2's) and groups it into runs of one group. A dependency the host hoisted out of its group makes its own run, so a group can head the list twice. Alternative: a second dependency walk in the webview, which could order a cycle differently from the host.\n5. **Proposed view in 2g:** a minimal `sessionOverlay`, built from `SessionView.board` only (masked while the results are hidden, with the neutral chip on hidden targets, no diff marks). This is what makes the session bar's Current | Proposed switch and §5.2's switch at the first stage work. Until 2h, Claude's arrows look like ordinary drawn arrows when the results are shown; 2h replaces this with `model/sessionBoard.ts`. Alternative: no Proposed view until 2h.\n6. **Group decisions:**\n   - A group Accept sends every selected item. Hidden Results are never selectable, so they are never in the group.\n   - A group Decline sends only what `planGroupDecline` gives.\n   - The \"Left N\" note combines what the webview left out and the host's `review.left`.\n   - \"Accept N\" is disabled when the preview takes nothing; its tooltip says why.\n\n   Alternative: send the group anyway and show the host's answer.\n7. **Decline menu:**\n   - It opens inline, built from the host's options.\n   - Reject declines at once; Shaky shows its note field and its own \"Decline (Shaky)\" button.\n   - The note is offered for every Shaky decline, including a Result's.\n   - \"Ask me instead\" declines the items the report entry names, or else that step's statement items.\n\n   Alternatives: no note on a Result's Shaky; prefill Transform, as RV-10 words it (Transform waits for slice 4).\n8. **Keys:** handled only on the focused listbox, with propagation stopped. Ctrl/Cmd+Z and Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+Z there act on the session stack. Global routing (`undoScope`, the header's Undo) stays with 2h. Alternative: no Undo key in 2g.\n9. **Read-only and busy (defence in depth):**\n   - Every control has a pure model that is closed with D2-62's text while a step runs, even if a host gate is open.\n   - One session request at a time; Exit is exempt (AF14), but only one Exit at a time.\n   - Apply is also blocked by the board unless the check passed, no file drifts and nothing is being judged.\n   - The Exit dialog's counts update with each session message, and the dialog closes once Apply runs.\n\n   Alternative: trust the host's gates alone.\n10. **Report:** the band comes from the host's report, not from `bandsOf`; Claude's arrows are marked with their item's status. A target that was not proved shows Claude's gap plus `missingArrowHints`, without repeating cards the judgement already lists, and offers \"Select these arrows\". Nothing shows at stage 0. Alternative: `bandsOf` on the shown graph, as §5.4 words it.\n11. **Provenance (D-15):** item references render as labels in parts. Every other host text the panel shows goes through `markAgent`, using the session's `agentPhrases` (Claude's sentences in full and cut to 60 and 40 characters). Card names carry the node's `wordedBy`. Alternative: plain host strings.\n12. **Builder wording.** The plan quotes none of these texts, and no core text was added:\n    - status words \"declined (Reject)\", \"declined (Shaky)\" and \"declined\"; the chip \"interrupted\";\n    - verdicts \"✓ established\", \"proved, not established\" and \"not proved\";\n    - `FINAL_CHECK_RULE_LABEL`;\n    - \"Nothing to review.\";\n    - the \"activity withheld\" line;\n    - \"Decline (Shaky)\", \"Continue\", \"Un-reject\", \"(an earlier version, view only)\", \"(Claude's arrow: ‹glyph› ‹status›)\";\n    - \"replaces your proof: the previous proof\", \"Why (optional)\", \"(not on the board)\", and \"✗ Declined\" for an arrow's decline.\n\n## Effects outside the repo and my scratch dir\n- **Chrome temp folder in /tmp:** Playwright's Chrome ran with an isolated HOME/XDG in a short temp dir that `test/harness/chrome-tmp.ts` created under `/tmp`, because my TMPDIR is too long for Chrome's socket path. The global teardown deleted it after each run, and the home guard reported the real home unchanged every time.\n- **Local web server:** a server on 127.0.0.1:41739 (Playwright's webServer) ran during each spec and stopped afterwards.\n- **`/home/zhengyew/telelean/node_modules/.vite-temp`:** inside the repo but outside `packages/`. The folder already existed (created 07:26, before my session). Each vite build wrote and removed its bundled-config temp file there; the folder is empty now and only its mtime changed.\n- **systemd:** `capped.sh` created transient systemd --user scopes, which ended with each job.\n- **Nothing else:** no network, installs, git changes or Claude runs. HEAD is still 1473ca0 with nothing staged. dist and out are untouched, and none of my processes are left running.\n\n## Things 2h or the integrator should know (not mine to change)\n- 2h should replace my minimal `sessionOverlay` with its `model/sessionBoard.ts` version, which adds marks and the proposed-arrow styling.\n- The prompt box still says slice 1's core text, \"An edit session is active: the board can't be edited until you accept or discard it.\". In slice 2 the actions are Apply or Exit.\n- Core's `reportSummaryShown`/`reportSummaryHidden` say \"1 targets\" for a single target.\n\nEverything else is in `/tmp/claude-1002/-home-zhengyew-telelean/c398a83b-d60f-46a4-ad9a-8d926e6fdd1b/scratchpad/b2g/`: original backups in `orig/`, mutation scripts and results in `mut/`, the scratch bundle in `webview-out/`, and screenshots in `test-results/`."